.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH terminal-of-tinsel-tonight 1  "tonight " 
.SH NAME
terminal\-of\-tinsel\-tonight \- See tonight\*(Aqs Christmas double bill
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBterminal\-of\-tinsel tonight\fR [\fB\-\-date\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-color\fR] [\fB\-\-shuffle\fR] [\fB\-\-pack\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Print a ticket for tonight\*(Aqs Channel 25 double bill. The line\-up changes every night, so check back tomorrow, or use \-\-shuffle for a different bill. From 1 to 24 December the guest behind that night\*(Aqs advent door tops the bill.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-date\fR \fI<YYYY\-MM\-DD>\fR
See the bill for another night (YYYY\-MM\-DD)
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print the command\*(Aqs data as JSON instead of drawing it (errors become a JSON object on stderr)
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-color\fR
Plain output: no colour, no emoji, ASCII borders (also set by NO_COLOR, or by piping)
.TP
\fB\-\-shuffle\fR
Pick a random double bill instead of tonight\*(Aqs
.TP
\fB\-\-pack\fR \fI<PACK>\fR
Only use creatures from these packs, e.g. \-\-pack nordic,dickens
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
